e, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le15ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Would Rather for What is Preferable"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the expression <span class=\"strong italic\">would rather</span> to ask for or express preference. We generally used its contracted form (<span class=\"strong italic\">'d rather</span>), followed by the basic or infinitive form of the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I would rather celebrate music and life in unison with an entire city!</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">You'd rather enjoy the summer while it lasts!</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I'd rather warn you though: you might want to come back every year after that!</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the expression in its negative form, too. For this, you use the expression <span class=\"strong italic\">not</span> right after <span class=\"italic\">would rather</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">We'd rather not be in crowded places.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">You'd rather not miss the festival.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I'd rather not take the whole day at the festival.</span></li></ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Questions With How + adjective"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">How + adjective</span> in a question if you want to know how someone or something is."}, {"type": "example", "content": "How breathtaking is it to feel the emotions of a jazz solo? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "How idyllic was that moment? "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "breathtaking "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "astonishing and awe-inspiring "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This jazz performance is breathtaking."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about a jazz festival."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "solo "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a part in a musical piece where one instrument plays unaccompanied "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This saxophone solo was amazing!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "experimental "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "involving a new and innovative style "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm a fan of experimental jazz!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "conventional "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " following a traditional style  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I prefer conventional blues music."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "joyful "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling great happiness "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Joyful children were running around."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob10aud05"}], "typ